{"id":"metizolam","name":"Metizolam","form":"tablet","status":"Well-documented","aliases":"metiz, desmethyletizolam","category":"Depressant","chemicalClass":"Thienodiazepines","psychoactiveClass":"Depressant","addictionPotential":"extremely addictive","toxicity":["large therapeutic index and margin of safety"],"summarySources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","summary":"The drug is also known as desmethyletizolam. It is a thienodiazepine with similar effects and structure to etizolam. In comparison to etizolam it is roughly half as potent with around a 60% longer half-life. The drug is a sedative hypnotic and may cause amnesia and lowered inhibitions in excess.","doseMaxTick":10,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"PsychonautWiki","unit":"mg","light":"1–2 mg","common":"2–4 mg","strong":"4–6 mg","heavy":"6 mg+","commonEstimate":3,"band":{"low":2,"high":4},"domain":[0.8,8.8],"segments":{"light":[1,2],"common":[2,4],"strong":[4,6],"heavy":[6,8.45]}}],"durationSources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"30–90 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"10–30 h","total":"5–8 h"}],"tolerance":{"buildUp":"within a couple of days of repeated administration","reset":"1 - 2 weeks","milestones":[{"label":"Full tolerance","value":"within a couple of days of repeated administration","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Half tolerance","value":"3 - 7 days","tone":"warning"},{"label":"Baseline","value":"1 - 2 weeks","tone":"positive"}],"crossTolerances":[{"group":"Cross-tolerance","items":["Thienzodiazepines","Benzodiazepines"]}]},"subjectiveEffects":[{"name":"Amnesia","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Amnesia"},{"name":"Analysis suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Analysis_suppression"},{"name":"Anxiety suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Anxiety_suppression"},{"name":"Cognitive euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Cognitive_euphoria"},{"name":"Compulsive redosing","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Compulsive_redosing"},{"name":"Delusions","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Delusions"},{"name":"Disinhibition","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Disinhibition"},{"name":"Dizziness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Dizziness"},{"name":"Emotion suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Emotion_suppression"},{"name":"Information processing suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Information_processing_suppression"},{"name":"Motor control loss","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Motor_control_loss"},{"name":"Muscle relaxation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Muscle_relaxation"},{"name":"Respiratory depression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Respiratory_depression"},{"name":"Sedation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Sedation"},{"name":"Thought deceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_deceleration"}],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Metizolam"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/metizolam"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metizolam"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on Metizolam","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21098977"}],"wikidata":"Q21098977","pharmacology":{"text":"Thienzodiazepines produce a variety of effects by binding to the benzodiazepine receptor site and magnifying the efficiency and effects of the neurotransmitter gamma aminobutyric acid (GABA) by acting on its receptors. As this site is the most prolific inhibitory receptor set within the brain, its modulation results in the sedating (or calming effects) of metizolam on the nervous system.","source":"PsychonautWiki","page":"Metizolam","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Metizolam#Pharmacology"},"uses":{"routes":"Oral, sublingual, rectal","figures":"Metizolam"}}